{
  "name": "Rebuild product-focused reels shot by shot with Apify, Gemini and fal.ai",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1328,
        -512
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Rebuild a reel shot by shot around your product\n\n### How it works\n\nYou give it a reel that already works, and the product you want to sell. It gives you back the same video, shot for shot, with your product in it.\n\nMost reel cloners watch a video once and generate something that feels similar. This one takes the reel apart. It finds every cut, pulls one frame from each shot, and studies them one at a time: how close the camera sits, what angle it looks from, how it moves, where the light falls. Then it rebuilds each shot around your product and puts the pieces back in the original order, each trimmed to the length it was before.\n\nSo a reel with three cuts comes back with three cuts, in the same rhythm. Whatever made the original hold attention is still holding it. Only the product changed.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Add three Header Auth credentials: Apify, Google Gemini and fal.ai.\n- [ ] Open **Set Source Reel And Target Product**. Paste the reel URL, describe your product. That is the only node you need to touch.\n- [ ] Press execute, or send a reel and product to the webhook from wherever you already work.\n\n### Customization\n\nMissing a cut you wanted? Lower `scene_threshold`. Getting more shots than the reel really has? Raise it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -768,
        -304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 528,
        "content": "## Collect what you are working with\nStart it by hand, or send a reel and a product to the webhook. Either way it lands here, where the reel URL, your product and the cut sensitivity are set."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -224,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Get the reel\nApify pulls down the source reel, then hands it to the scene splitter to work out where the cuts are."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        240,
        -128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Wait for the cuts\nScene detection runs in the background. This checks every ten seconds and loops until it is done, so long reels never time out mid-run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note4",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        912,
        -240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Pull one frame per shot\nThe finished report is split into individual scenes, and the single frame that represents each shot is downloaded ready for reading."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note5",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1616,
        -272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 592,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Read every shot\nAll the frames go to Gemini together. It reads the framing, angle, movement and lighting of each shot, then writes what that shot looks like with your product in it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note6",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2240,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 368,
        "content": "## Rebuild each shot\nOne scene at a time: a new still is generated from the shot description, then sent off to be animated with the movement that shot originally had."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note7",
      "name": "Sticky Note7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2944,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Wait for each clip\nAnimation takes a while, so this polls until the clip is ready, collects it, and goes back round for the next scene."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note8",
      "name": "Sticky Note8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2240,
        -432
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 272,
        "content": "## Lay out the timeline\nOnce every scene is done, the clips go back in the original order and each is trimmed to the length of the shot it replaces."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note9",
      "name": "Sticky Note9",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2688,
        -432
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 592,
        "height": 272,
        "content": "## Wait for the final render\nThe assembly job is polled the same way, until the finished video is ready to collect."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note10",
